<content><![CDATA[<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>
<multiple-choice question="What does a UV map do?" single-option="" randomize="">
  <input type="checkbox" value="It maps each point on a 3D surface to a position on a 2D texture" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="It sets the color of the lights">
  <input type="checkbox" value="It stores the model's polygon count">
  <input type="checkbox" value="It controls the render resolution">
</multiple-choice>
<true-false-question question="In a PBR metallic workflow, the roughness map controls how sharp or blurry reflections look.">
  <input type="checkbox" value="True" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="False">
</true-false-question>
<self-check title="Think it through">
  <p slot="question">A brick texture looks stretched on one side of your model. What would you check, and how might you fix it?</p>
  <p>Check the UV layout with a checker texture for stretched or distorted islands and uneven texel density. Fix it by adding or moving seams, re-unwrapping or relaxing those islands, and scaling them to a consistent density.</p>
</self-check>
